@startuml
title The calibration run of an asset class

start
:Read the class's calibration policy\n(window, variance window, inverse rule,\nprovider order, fallback);
repeat :Next feed of the class;
  :Resolve the feed's fixing item\nunder the policy;
  if (A fixing is found?) then (yes)
    :Measure the level and the spread\nover the policy's window;
    if (Applied?) then (yes)
      :Write the level and the deviations\nas a new version of the feed;
    endif
    if (The feed's variance is GJR-GARCH?) then (yes)
      :Read the variance window\nof the same item;
      :Capture the points:\neach fixing as stored, its return in\nmarket convention, or why it is left out;
      :Fit GJR-GARCH to the used returns\n(variance targeting, Gaussian QMLE);
      if (Enough returns and an admissible shape?) then (yes)
        :State: proposed;
      else (no)
        :State: rejected, with the reason;
      endif
      if (Applied?) then (yes)
        :Store the input, its points and the\ncalibration once, under ids named\nby what identifies them;
      endif
    endif
  else (no)
    :Keep the fixed level, or refuse,\nas the policy's fallback says;
  endif
repeat while (More feeds?) is (yes)
:Report every feed: its start,\nits changes and its variance calibration;
stop
@enduml
